WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.300
[MUSIC]

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:10.298
So a few months ago, I was cleaning
out the attic of my childhood home,

00:00:10.298 --> 00:00:13.815
when I stumbled across
my eighth grade journal.

00:00:13.815 --> 00:00:18.462
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; In eighth grade I had buck teeth,

00:00:18.462 --> 00:00:21.959
size 11 shoes, and
long skinny toothpick legs.

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:25.520
I opened the journal,
and dusted it off, and

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:27.290
found one particularly interesting entry.

00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:30.780
It was about what my life
would be like at age 30.

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:36.765
In eighth grade I predicted that by
now I would be married with two kids.

00:00:36.765 --> 00:00:38.780
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; Play professional football for

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:39.859
the Denver Broncos.

00:00:39.859 --> 00:00:42.890
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; And own a self-driving car.

00:00:45.470 --> 00:00:48.150
See, when I was young,
I wanted to be an astronaut.

00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:51.600
I wanted to be the second Neil
to step foot on the moon.

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:53.470
The first doctor to cure cancer.

00:00:55.270 --> 00:01:01.050
But as I got older, voices and doubts
told me I wasn't going to play football.

00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:05.120
That being an astronaut,
that's not a reasonable career.

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:07.320
And a cure in cancer?

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:08.590
Good luck.

00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:13.360
These voices still plague me today.

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:20.780
Outer critic says, you can't work at
x company, they only hire engineers.

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:24.150
And when I think about raising my hand in
class, I immediately put it down because

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:26.645
I'm worried that what I'm
going to say isn't smart enough.

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:38.059
The voices, the voices in my head,
keep me wishing and

00:01:38.059 --> 00:01:41.760
wanting rather than daring and doing.

00:01:43.330 --> 00:01:44.870
But I realized I'm not alone.

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:48.620
I conducted a survey and
asked over 50 people this one question.

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:50.010
I wish I had the courage to.

00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:52.781
One of my friends said,

00:01:52.781 --> 00:01:56.650
I wish I had the courage to bring up
an uncomfortable topic at the GSB.

00:01:58.330 --> 00:02:00.870
That I wouldn't be judged for saying it.

00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:06.100
Another person said, I wish I had the
courage to leave my high paying job and

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:06.890
start a company.

00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:12.990
Another person said I wish I had
the courage to tell my parents I am gay.

00:02:15.810 --> 00:02:19.050
What do you wish you
had the courage to do?

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:26.360
See the problem is these voices of doubt,
of fear.

00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:27.750
They're crippling our relationships.

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:30.520
They're hindering our potential.

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:36.610
They're telling us, you know what get back
in line, play it safe, follow the heard.

00:02:36.610 --> 00:02:41.700
See, the opposite of courage is
not cowardice, it's conformity.

00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:46.850
The opposite of courage is not cowardice,
it's conformity.

00:02:48.050 --> 00:02:51.110
There is something about finding my
eighth grade journal that brought me back

00:02:51.110 --> 00:02:52.250
to my junior year of college.

00:02:52.250 --> 00:02:57.990
It was a cold winter night and I was
in an empty college football stadium.

00:02:57.990 --> 00:02:59.899
I was cleaning it because
I was earning money.

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:02.270
Because I was a student at BYU.

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:06.330
I swept soggy popcorn and

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:09.880
half eaten burritos with other trash,
I collected it by hand.

00:03:10.970 --> 00:03:13.065
I looked up from the trash
at the empty field.

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:18.750
What happened to the dreams I had
as a kid to play college football?

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:28.120
See, voices told me, voices of fear,
of doubt, you know what?

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:31.420
You're a junior now,
you can't play division one football.

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:33.590
Especially not a team that's
ranked seventh in the nation.

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:38.980
One kid said dude,
you're not going to play in the NFL.

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:41.260
So why don't you spend your
time looking for a job?

00:03:45.168 --> 00:03:49.793
Couple weeks passed, and
my roommate Josh, he entered my room

00:03:49.793 --> 00:03:54.520
where I was laying on my bed resigned
to my current place in life.

00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:58.749
NeaI, I signed you up for try outs
he said as he handed me the paper.

00:04:00.290 --> 00:04:00.790
You can do it.

00:04:02.020 --> 00:04:06.770
I realized that it was easier to not
try out, then to try out and fail.

00:04:06.770 --> 00:04:08.740
But I remember the words
of my high school coach.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:13.750
There's no should of, would of,
could of, there's only, I did.

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:21.270
So despite enormous doubt
given my limited eligibility,

00:04:21.270 --> 00:04:24.390
my small stature, my just all this doubt.

00:04:25.570 --> 00:04:29.460
I courageously confronted my fear,
and tried out.

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:31.715
And to be honest,
it felt a little bit like this.

00:04:31.715 --> 00:04:40.770
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]

00:04:40.770 --> 00:04:42.800
&gt;&gt; It's not the outcome that mattered.

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:47.430
But for me, it was that I faced my
fear and did something I wanted to do.

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:54.180
I made a team that winter
only to be cut in spring.

00:04:57.050 --> 00:05:00.570
But with new found conviction that
what I was doing mattered to me.

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:04.020
It didn't matter what anybody else said,
it mattered to me.

00:05:06.220 --> 00:05:10.720
I attacked 5 AM workouts in
an abandoned field near my house.

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:13.420
I ran sprints,
ran up stairs until I wanted to puke.

00:05:16.140 --> 00:05:19.290
I came back that fall,
I tried out again, and I made the team.

00:05:23.844 --> 00:05:29.220
I remember standing on the field after
the final game under the lights.

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:32.430
I looked up into the stands.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:37.740
Where just a season before,
I was cleaning up trash.

00:05:40.580 --> 00:05:41.538
I can't believe, I almost didn't try out.

00:05:46.920 --> 00:05:50.460
Satisfaction came from
being true to myself.

00:05:52.510 --> 00:05:53.010
What matters to you?

00:05:55.810 --> 00:05:57.990
What are you committed to?

00:05:57.990 --> 00:06:00.720
Do you find yourself wanting and wishing?

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:02.740
Or daring and doing?

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:11.880
Do you find yourself standing in
the stands or playing on the field?

00:06:18.630 --> 00:06:23.706
It's been said that if what
we believe is different

00:06:23.706 --> 00:06:27.730
than what we do, we will never be happy.

00:06:28.760 --> 00:06:33.120
If what we believe is different than
what we do, we will never be happy.

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:36.500
Steve Jobs said it like this,
your time is limited,

00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:38.660
so don't waste it living
someone else's life.

00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:43.940
Don't let the voice of other's opinion
drown out your own inner voice.

00:06:43.940 --> 00:06:47.840
And have the courage to be true
to your heart and intuition.

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:51.120
They somehow already know what
you want to truly become.

00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:52.240
Everything else is secondary.

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:54.759
You know what's interesting
about Steve Jobs?

00:06:56.810 --> 00:06:57.310
He was cut from his team.

00:07:00.380 --> 00:07:02.550
Think about Thomas Edison.

00:07:02.550 --> 00:07:05.420
His teacher said,
you're not smart enough to learn.

00:07:06.600 --> 00:07:10.255
Walt Disney was fired from the newspaper
for lacking imagination and creativity.

00:07:10.255 --> 00:07:13.990
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; These were people who were

00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:15.989
committed to something
greater than their fear.

00:07:18.890 --> 00:07:24.030
It's funny to me to think about what would
a world be like if Jobs had given up?

00:07:24.030 --> 00:07:25.936
If Edison and Disney had listened?

00:07:25.936 --> 00:07:32.285
No phones, no lights, no Lion King.

00:07:32.285 --> 00:07:35.844
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; No Mufasa, hakuna matata, no Goofy,

00:07:35.844 --> 00:07:36.840
no Donald Duck.

00:07:45.430 --> 00:07:50.674
Hanging in my bedroom wall
next to where my eighth grade

00:07:50.674 --> 00:07:56.150
journal now sits is a quote that
I look to when I face fear.

00:07:57.920 --> 00:08:00.820
It's kind of long and
you probably heard it before.

00:08:02.070 --> 00:08:05.542
But I want you to think about one thing
that you wish you were doing now, but

00:08:05.542 --> 00:08:06.220
you're not.

00:08:09.810 --> 00:08:15.179
Teddy Roosevelt said this,
it's not the critic who counts.

00:08:16.730 --> 00:08:20.120
Not the man who points out where
the strong man stumbled, or

00:08:20.120 --> 00:08:21.800
where the doer of deeds
could have done them better.

00:08:23.150 --> 00:08:27.150
The credit belongs to the man
who is actually in the arena.

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:30.190
Whose face is marred with dust and
sweat and blood.

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:31.900
Who strives valiantly.

00:08:31.900 --> 00:08:34.740
Who errs and comes short again and again.

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:37.900
Who knows the great enthusiasms,
the great devotions.

00:08:37.900 --> 00:08:39.560
Who spends himself in a worthy cause, and

00:08:39.560 --> 00:08:44.640
who at worst if fails at least
fails while daring greatly.

00:08:47.120 --> 00:08:50.300
So that his place shall
never be with those cold and

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:54.050
timid souls who know neither victory or
defeat.

00:08:56.600 --> 00:09:02.290
My ask of you,
when voices of doubt and fear

00:09:02.290 --> 00:09:07.750
enter your mind, when critics tell you
you can't, go ahead and do it anyways.

00:09:10.050 --> 00:09:15.712
Dare to leave the stands and
enter the arena,

00:09:15.712 --> 00:09:23.610
because real satisfaction comes
from being true to yourself.

00:09:23.610 --> 00:09:25.422
Thank you.

00:09:25.422 --> 00:09:26.439
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]
[MUSIC]

